module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_prefix_read_unfolds_the_whole_text_on_every_window_attempt

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }

data a_prefix_read_unfolds_the_whole_text_on_every_window_attempt: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_prefix_read_unfolds_the_whole_text_on_every_window_attempt" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a reader that needs only the start of a text pays for the whole text. v2.compiler.tokenize tokenize_prefix_prepared stops its WALK at a scalar limit, but its first step is `unicode_scalar_unfold(s: text)` over the WHOLE text, and v2.compiler.module_header module_header_read_window calls it once per window attempt (the window starts at module_header_first_window and doubles until the header production settles). So the unfold is O(file) per attempt while the walk it feeds is O(window): the prefix door made the lex proportional to the header and left the text ingress proportional to the file. A header that settles in the first window still unfolds every scalar of its file.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. It is not the lex (the walk is windowed) and not the production (the tail is derived once per run by v2.compiler.grammar_reach grammar_production_tail). The unfold is std.coercion unicode_scalar_unfold, the declared host-text to code-point-sequence crossing (DESIGN section 4, ruling `text_crossings_go_through_the_unfold`), and it takes the whole String: there is no declared form of the crossing that yields only the leading scalars. A caller that wants a window therefore has no route that does not materialize the rest, and a knob on the existing unfold would give one name two contracts (DESIGN section 3, meaning fork). DERIVED from the code, NOT measured per verb: the live-roots step prints one line for both `check-layout` and `parse-population`.",

    "MEASURED, the step it sits in: the v2-native-cli step from `population controls - check-layout and parse-population over the live roots` to `live roots - check-layout held`, 2026-10-13. #13866 at adca9d6b (run 38378591395): 907.9 s. Six trees carrying #13842 without #13866: 1030.0 to 1137.6 s (median 1076). Two trees before #13842: 786.5 and 861.9 s. So #13866 recovered about 168 s of the median and the step is about 28 s over the roughly 880 s ceiling, with 46 to 122 s of #13842's cost still present. This row is one named candidate for that remainder (the fold driver over the grammar tables is the other); neither is attributed by a per-verb measurement yet.",

    "HARM: DESIGN section 6, bare minimum cost: a proven cost-shape defect is always fixed regardless of realized n, because n is small here is not time-stable. Here n is every module of the live roots (8317 at the measurement) per verb, in a job that is one required context.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable (the cost is bounded by the file and the answer is correct). ATTAINABLE CEILING for THIS instance: the door's text ingress cannot exceed the window by construction, because a windowed unfold is a distinct declared coercion plan in std.coercion (the leading scalars of the whole unfold, the remainder never materialized) and is the only route the prefix door has. The CLASS, a prefix consumer paying for its whole input, is a cost shape and stays a ratchet: it is observed by the step time, not decided by a wall. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, the capability restored: the windowed unfold declared in std.coercion with an inhabitance control that its scalars equal the whole unfold's prefix of the same length, tokenize_prefix_prepared consuming it, and the live-roots step re-measured with the same extraction. Ordered by tidy-ant-251 as its own PR after #13866."
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.tokenize", decl_name: "tokenize_prefix_prepared", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.module_header", decl_name: "module_header_read_window", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.coercion", decl_name: "unicode_scalar_unfold", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
